WEBVTT

NOTE RJ Tech English captions derived from the original bilingual track.

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:09.900
Feed the powered-trailer harness through the indicated opening toward the rear of the vehicle.

2
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:18.440
Install the trailer connector in the rear metal bracket and secure it.

3
00:00:27.728 --> 00:00:31.628
Confirm the trailer connector orientation and locking position.

4
00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:54.280
Use 16 mm clamps to secure the trailer harness along the frame.

5
00:00:55.675 --> 00:01:01.075
Use the exact mounting locations shown in the video.

6
00:01:20.697 --> 00:01:23.975
Tighten the clamps with the powered tool.

7
00:01:38.093 --> 00:01:48.292
Route the battery charging harness from the front to the rear along the path shown.

8
00:01:52.146 --> 00:01:55.446
Mount the charging inlet in the indicated position.

9
00:02:00.843 --> 00:02:08.978
Recheck the charging-inlet position and orientation.

10
00:02:42.718 --> 00:02:44.908
Locate the signal connector on the low-voltage harness.

11
00:02:56.973 --> 00:03:03.973
Install the signal connector at the mounting position shown.

12
00:03:38.583 --> 00:03:47.583
Secure the charging and low-voltage harnesses together with 16 mm clamps.

13
00:04:38.526 --> 00:04:47.617
Connect the charging harness to the battery interface marked for charging.

14
00:04:52.217 --> 00:04:59.207
Connect the positive and negative trailer leads to the matching battery output interface.

15
00:05:05.481 --> 00:05:07.681
After checking the markings: orange to orange, black to black.

16
00:05:08.481 --> 00:05:13.381
A click confirms that the connector is locked in place.

17
00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:23.681
Arrange the harnesses inside the compartment without sharp bends or pinching.

18
00:05:33.841 --> 00:05:37.741
Refit the battery-compartment cover.

19
00:05:53.009 --> 00:05:54.992
Install and snug the cover screws.

20
00:06:04.522 --> 00:06:10.922
Tighten all four cover mounting points evenly.
